                <h1 class="content-title">Service Operations <span class="gradient-text">Workspace (SOW)</span></h1>
                <p class="content-subtitle">
                    Master modern Service Desk operations in the Next Experience — unified ITSM &amp; ITOM workflows, 
                    Advanced Work Assignment (AWA), Interaction management, Agent Assist, and Now Assist Generative AI.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Section 1: Next Experience Unification -->
            <section class="content-section" id="sow-mission">
                <h2>Next Experience Architecture &amp; ITSM + ITOM Unification</h2>
                <p>
                    <strong>Service Operations Workspace (SOW)</strong> represents the modern evolution of the ServiceNow agent experience, 
                    replacing legacy UI16 forms and disjointed list views with a purpose-built, high-density configurable workspace.
                </p>
                <p>
                    SOW's primary architectural breakthrough is the <strong>unification of ITSM (Service Desk)</strong> and 
                    <strong>ITOM (IT Operations Management)</strong>: Service Desk agents and Operations engineers view user-reported 
                    incidents side-by-side with real-time server telemetry, ITOM Event Management alerts, and active CMDB outage maps.
                </p>

                <div class="feature-grid">
                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>Multi-Tab Session Cockpit</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Resolvers can manage multiple active live chats, incident investigations, and CI records simultaneously 
                            within a single unified browser session without losing draft inputs or switching tabs.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>Configurable UI Builder Canvas</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Built on ServiceNow's modern Seismic component framework and UI Builder, allowing administrators 
                            to customize ribbons, sidebars, and widget placements dynamically per persona.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Section 2: Table Architecture & Schema -->
            <section class="content-section" id="table-schema">
                <h2>Table Architecture & Key Fields</h2>
                <p>
                    SOW leverages specialized foundational tables for session routing, channel presence, and interaction management:
                </p>

                <table class="data-table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Table Name</th>
                            <th>Parent Extension</th>
                            <th>Operational Scope</th>
                            <th>Key Columns</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><code>interaction</code></td>
                            <td>None (Base Table)</td>
                            <td>Omnichannel landing record created for live chats, calls, and walk-ups before task creation.</td>
                            <td><code>number</code>, <code>channel_metadata_document</code>, <code>type</code> (Chat, Phone, Walk-up), <code>state</code>, <code>assigned_to</code></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><code>awa_service_channel</code></td>
                            <td>None (Base Table)</td>
                            <td>Defines work streams routed through AWA (e.g. Live Chat, Incidents, Cases).</td>
                            <td><code>name</code>, <code>table</code>, <code>capacity_mode</code>, <code>max_capacity</code></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><code>awa_queue</code></td>
                            <td>None (Base Table)</td>
                            <td>Routing queues prioritized by skill requirements and customer VIP tiers.</td>
                            <td><code>name</code>, <code>service_channel</code>, <code>priority</code>, <code>schedule</code></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><code>awa_work_item</code></td>
                            <td>None (Base Table)</td>
                            <td>Individual queue payload assigned to an active resolver agent.</td>
                            <td><code>document_id</code> (Ref to ticket), <code>assigned_to</code>, <code>state</code> (Queued, Offered, Accepted, Rejected)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><code>cmn_rota</code></td>
                            <td>None (Base Table)</td>
                            <td>On-Call roster schedules and shift rotations.</td>
                            <td><code>name</code>, <code>group</code> (Ref to <code>sys_user_group</code>), <code>schedule</code></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </section>

            <!-- Section 3: Interaction Management -->
            <section class="content-section" id="interaction-mgmt">
                <h2>The Interaction Management Framework (<code>interaction</code>)</h2>
                <p>
                    Historically, every incoming phone call or chat created an <code>incident</code> record immediately, leading to 
                    database bloat from false alarms or quick password resets. SOW introduces the <strong>Interaction (<code>interaction</code>)</strong> table:
                </p>

                <div class="feature-grid">
                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>Omnichannel Ingestion Envelope</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Incoming communications from Microsoft Teams, Virtual Agent, OpenFrame Telephony (CTI), or Walk-up desks 
                            instantly create an <code>interaction</code> record holding the live transcript and caller metadata.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>One-Click Ticket Promotion</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            If an interaction represents a genuine outage or service need, agents click <em>"Create Incident"</em> or 
                            <em>"Create Request"</em>, automatically linking the interaction and copying the conversation transcript into work notes.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Section 4: Advanced Work Assignment (AWA) -->
            <section class="content-section" id="awa-routing">
                <h2>Advanced Work Assignment (AWA) Omnichannel Engine</h2>
                <p>
                    <strong>Advanced Work Assignment (AWA)</strong> automatically routes incoming interactions, incidents, 
                    and catalog tasks to the best-suited agent based on availability, capacity, and certified skills:
                </p>

                <div class="diagram-block">
                    <div class="diagram-title">AWA Omnichannel Routing &amp; Resolution Lifecycle</div>
                    <div class="mermaid">
                    graph TD
                        INCOMING["Incoming Omnichannel Request<br>(Virtual Agent Chat, Phone Call, or P1 Incident)"] --> QUEUE["AWA Routing Queue (awa_queue)<br>Evaluates Priority & Language/Skill Requirements"]
                        
                        QUEUE --> CAPACITY["Agent Capacity & Presence Engine<br>Checks ava_presence_state (Available) & Open Workload"]
                        
                        CAPACITY --> OFFER["Work Item Offered (awa_work_item)<br>Desktop screen pop & audio chime with 30s acceptance timer"]
                        
                        OFFER -->|Agent Accepts| COCKPIT["Launch Service Operations Workspace Cockpit<br>Transcript & Customer Profile populated automatically"]
                        OFFER -->|Timer Expires / Rejected| REROUTE["Re-route to Next Qualified Resolver"]
                        REROUTE --> CAPACITY
                        
                        COCKPIT --> ASSIST["Agent Assist Surfaces Matching KB Articles & Similar Outages"]
                        ASSIST --> RESOLVE["Ticket Resolved & Interaction Closed"]
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="tabs-container">
                    <div class="tabs-header">
                        <button class="tab-btn active" data-tab="tab-awa-routing">Routing Criteria</button>
                        <button class="tab-btn" data-tab="tab-awa-presence">Presence &amp; Capacity</button>
                    </div>

                    <div class="tab-panel active" id="tab-awa-routing">
                        <h3>AWA Routing Allocation Methods</h3>
                        <table class="data-table">
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Routing Method</th>
                                    <th>Operational Behavior</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Most Capacity</strong></td>
                                    <td>Routes to the qualified agent currently carrying the lowest percentage of their maximum allowed work items.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Last Assigned (Round Robin)</strong></td>
                                    <td>Routes to the qualified agent who has gone the longest time without receiving a new work item.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Skill-Based Routing</strong></td>
                                    <td>Matches required ticket skills (e.g. <code>Oracle DBA Level 3</code>, <code>German Language</code>) with agent certifications (<code>cmn_skill</code>).</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>

                    <div class="tab-panel" id="tab-awa-presence">
                        <h3>Agent Presence States</h3>
                        <p>Agents manage their availability via the SOW status drawer:</p>
                        <ul class="feature-bullet-list">
                            <li><strong>Available:</strong> Actively accepting live chat, phone, and incident screen pops.</li>
                            <li><strong>Busy / In a Meeting:</strong> Temporarily pauses new push allocations while preserving current active work items.</li>
                            <li><strong>Offline:</strong> Agent logged off; no work routed.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Section 5: Agent Assist & Now Assist -->
            <section class="content-section" id="agent-assist">
                <h2>Agent Assist &amp; Now Assist Generative AI</h2>
                <p>
                    Embedded directly within the right-hand panel of SOW, <strong>Agent Assist</strong> provides 
                    real-time intelligence as the resolver works the ticket:
                </p>

                <div class="feature-grid">
                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>Contextual Recommendations</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Continuously runs contextual queries on the ticket's Short Description and CI to surface matching 
                            <strong>Knowledge Articles</strong>, <strong>Known Errors</strong>, and <strong>Historically Resolved Incidents</strong>.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>Now Assist (Generative AI)</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            • <strong>Chat Summarization:</strong> Generates concise incident descriptions from long customer live chat transcripts in seconds.<br>
                            • <strong>Resolution Notes Generation:</strong> Auto-drafts complete technical close notes summarizing the troubleshooting steps taken.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Section 6: CI Health & Topology Ribbon -->
            <section class="content-section" id="ci-health-ribbon">
                <h2>Service &amp; CI Health Ribbon</h2>
                <p>
                    At the top of every incident in SOW, the <strong>Ribbon Component</strong> provides instantaneous operational awareness:
                </p>
                <ul class="feature-bullet-list">
                    <li><strong>Upstream Business Service Health:</strong> Displays whether the CI's parent Business Offering is experiencing active outages or degraded performance.</li>
                    <li><strong>Recent Changes on CI:</strong> Lists changes deployed on the target server within the past 72 hours, allowing resolvers to immediately pinpoint change-induced outages.</li>
                    <li><strong>Caller VIP &amp; History Badge:</strong> Highlights caller tier, open ticket counts, and contact preferences.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

